  "prompt": "Create an ORIGINAL production sprite sheet for Theandril, a gritty dark-fantasy hex strategy game about hearthland communities after the fall of the Witness Roads.\nExact sheet layout: 4 columns by 3 rows of equal square cells, no gutters, on a genuinely transparent background. Each cell is a 64 by 64 logical-pixel canvas shown at identical integer enlargement. Total logical sheet 256 x 192. Every figure fully contained inside its cell with generous transparent margins, feet on the same baseline at logical y=56, centered x=32. Orthographic three-quarter front view facing southeast, slightly seen from above, NOT isometric floor bases. No labels, grid lines, ground patches, shadows outside silhouette, text or watermarks.\nRow 1: SAME Oathguard in four genuinely different restrained idle breathing frames: weathered charcoal iron helmet, narrow eye slit, brown padded coat, bone-colored scarf, sturdy boots, short worn sword down in right hand and small angular buckler in left. Stocky adult human realistic proportions, NOT chibi; no horns or copied game character.\nRow 2: SAME Wayfinder scout in four restrained idle breathing frames: hooded olive wool cloak, leather bracers, travel pack, bow held diagonally, arrow quiver, face partly shadowed, lean adult human.\nRow 3: SAME Hearthcaravan in four idle frames: weathered small two-wheeled handcart with covered ash canvas, crates, old brass oath bell, and one hooded adult traveler walking beside it. Clear wagon/traveler silhouette, not a horse or knight.\nVisual style: authentic carefully hand-placed 64px pixel art, crisp square pixel clusters, hard edges, NO anti-aliasing, NO smooth gradients, NO blur, NO painterly texture, NO tiny dithering confetti. About 12-18 shared colors per row. Restrained charcoal/umber/oxidized iron/old bone palette with readable warm highlights. Northwest key light, dark but readable medium value bodies; serious worn fantasy craftsmanship. Animation registration and equipment identical throughout each row; only cloth/breathing posture subtle motion, feet remain planted. Make the whole sheet exact and useful as runtime game sprites, not a concept illustration.",
